{
  "kanda": "aranya",
  "sarga": 58,
  "title": "Rama anguishes for Seetha's aloneness",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga58/aranyasans58.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga58/aranyaitrans58.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Rama is anguished for Seetha's aloneness and it is expressed in his chastening Lakshmana. Rama asks him as to why he left Seetha unguarded in the lonely forest. Rama rushes rapidly to hermitage thinking and talking that rapidly to Lakshmana about Seetha, and on arriving he finds vacuity in hermitage and then he is thrown in throes of despair."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये अरण्य काण्डे अष्ट पंचाशः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 58th chapter in Aranya Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "3.58.1",
      "label": "3.58.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "स दृष्ट्वा लक्ष्मणम् दीनम् शून्यम् दशरथ आत्मजः |\nपर्यपृच्छत धर्माअत्मा वैदेहीम् आगतम् विना",
      "iast": "sa dṛṣṭvā lakṣmaṇam dīnam śūnyam daśaratha ātmajaḥ |\nparyapṛcchata dharmāatmā vaidehīm āgatam vinā",
      "translation": "On seeing dreary Lakshmana coming into the void of forest devoid of Vaidehi, then the virtue-souled Rama, the son of Dasharatha, has asked him impatiently.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "dharmaaatmaa",
          "iast": "dharmāatmā",
          "devanagari": "धर्माअत्मा",
          "meaning": "virtue-souled one",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "saH dasharatha aatmajaH",
          "iast": "saḥ daśaratha ātmajaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सः दशरथ आत्मजः",
          "meaning": "he that, Dasharatha's, son [Rama]",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shuunyam",
          "iast": "śūnyam",
          "devanagari": "शून्यं",
          "meaning": "void of [in void forest]",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaidehiim vinaa aagatam",
          "iast": "vaidehīm vinā āgatam",
          "devanagari": "वैदेहीं विना आगतं",
          "meaning": "Vaidehi, without [devoid of,] who has come",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "diinam lakSmaNam dR^iSTvaa",
          "iast": "dīnam lakṣmaṇam dṛṣṭvā",
          "devanagari": "दीनं लक्ष्मणं दृष्ट्वा",
          "meaning": "dreary, Lakshmana, on seeing",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pari apR^icChata",
          "iast": "pari apṛcchata",
          "devanagari": "परि अपृच्छत",
          "meaning": "verily [impatiently] asked.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.58.2",
      "label": "3.58.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "प्रस्थितम् दण्डक अरण्यम् या माम् अनुजगाम ह |\nक्व सा लक्ष्मण वैदेही याम् हित्वा त्वम् इह आगतः",
      "iast": "prasthitam daṇḍaka araṇyam yā mām anujagāma ha |\nkva sā lakṣmaṇa vaidehī yām hitvā tvam iha āgataḥ",
      "translation": "\"She who has come in tow with me to Dandaka forest when I started for peregrination, whom you have now deserted and came here, oh, Lakshmana, she that Vaidehi, where is she?",
